==Battleground==
*1 [[Sunfish Jones]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*10 [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>, delay 16.67~33.33 seconds<sup>500f~1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Angelic Sleipnir]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*1 [[Loris]] spawns after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.
*1 [[Loris]] spawns after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Loris]] spawns after 140 seconds<sup>4,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Since Loris has a 5-second curse uptime, the best counter is a level 40+ [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] as he can get into the Lorises' blind spots and avoid the curse (and can even completely nullify the danger of curse with his Resist Curse [[Talents|Talent]]). For damage, [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] is the most viable non-[[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] option here, but be careful when timing him as Angelic Sleipnir can easily stunlock him before he even lands one hit. It's recommended to spawn Bahamut early on (at least before the third Loris comes out) so he can be recharged again when the enemies start getting too close for comfort. A good Uber Rare Cat to bring is [[Urashima Taro (Uber Rare Cat)|King Gamereon]], who can just barely squeeze into the Lorises' blind spots too.

It's highly recommended to bring good stallers like [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Cleanerbot Cat]] as they can prevent them from pushing too hard. [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] can also help get damage in on Sleipnir. [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] and [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]] are important to make sure Ramen is spammable enough to be an effective meatshield; and if you feel your Ramen needs to be more tanky as well, throw in [[Vengeful Cat (Rare Cat)|Vengeful Cat]] and [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sadako Cat]] to activate [[Horror Movies (Combo)|Horror Movies]].

